# Accepted-risk vulnerability exceptions for the Trivy image scan
# (Docker Build Test job in .github/workflows/ci.yml). Mirrors .grype.yaml.
# Every entry needs a reason, an owner action and an expiry. See SECURITY.md,
# "Known accepted vulnerabilities".
#
# braces 3.0.3 - GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm / CVE-2026-93687 (High)
#   Stack-exhaustion denial of service via deeply nested brace patterns.
#   Why ignored: no fixed release exists. 3.0.3 is the latest published version
#   and the advisory lists no patched version. Dependency chain (every link is
#   already at its latest release): deepagents -> fast-glob / micromatch 4.0.8
#   -> braces ^3.0.3. Nothing we can bump or override cleanly.
#   Exposure: only reached through the AI agent's filesystem glob/grep tools,
#   whose patterns are model-generated (so a user prompt could influence them).
#   Impact is limited to a failed tool call: braces rejects inputs over 65,536
#   chars, and nested patterns up to that cap did not crash the process in a
#   manual check under Bun (micromatch 4.0.8).
#   Expiry: the exp: date makes this entry stop applying, so the scan goes red
#   again and forces a re-review. On expiry, check whether braces, micromatch or
#   deepagents shipped a fix, then remove this entry or renew with a new date.
CVE-2026-93687 exp:2027-01-31

# minimatch 3.1.4 - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 / CVE-2026-118764 (Medium)
#   Denial of service via globparts amplification.
#   Why ignored: the only patched release is 11.0.1, which removes the callable
#   CommonJS export. eslint 9, @eslint/eslintrc and eslint-plugin-react (all at
#   their latest releases) depend on minimatch ^3.1.2 and call
#   require("minimatch")(...), so overriding to 11 breaks `bun run lint`.
#   Exposure: dev-only lint tooling. It is not installed in the production
#   image (`bun install --production`), and it only evaluates glob patterns
#   from our own eslint.config.js, never user input.
#   Expiry: on expiry, check whether eslint / eslint-plugin-react moved to a
#   patched minimatch, then remove this entry or renew with a new date.
CVE-2026-118764 exp:2027-01-31
